WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.077
Note: Action -&gt; Inspiration -&gt; Motivation

00:00:00.077 --> 00:00:00.080
---

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:07.920
It's finally over! Or is it? Yeah it's&nbsp;
definitely over. Oooor is it though? Yeah.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.800
That's pretty much how I and probably&nbsp;
you as well felt about the conclusion to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.960
the raid on Onigashima we have gotten&nbsp;
with chapter 1050 [Spoiler Warning].

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.800
So is this the end of the&nbsp;
battle? Of Wano altogether?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:26.960
And what will happen next? While leaving a lot&nbsp;
of these questions open, we did get a couple of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.880
really important answers in this&nbsp;
chapter as well. Here's a quick recap:

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:37.200
After Luffy's dramatic final attack&nbsp;
with an island sized fist, that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:44.080
blasted Kaido into the ground, we get to see how&nbsp;
crazily powerful this punch of Luffy's gear 5th&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:50.880
truly was. It turns out that it carried such&nbsp;
incredible force, that it managed to drill Kaido&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:58.320
not only into the ground, but THROUGH the crust&nbsp;
of the earth into a magma cave that is revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:04.080
to be located directly beneath Wano. Not&nbsp;
only that, but it turns out Big Mom has had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:11.520
the very same fate after Law's and Kid's final&nbsp;
attacks. Which let's be real is pretty wild,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:17.360
even for One PIece, but I guess it goes to&nbsp;
show how powerful Luffy and co have become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.280
throughout Wano. Turns out the thing&nbsp;
the saw underneath onigashima wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:28.160
a hidden room full with poneglyphs and rare devil&nbsp;
fruits, but one full with molten flaming hot rock.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:34.720
Kaido and Big Mom seem to be literally sinking&nbsp;
into this pool of Magma, I think it's magma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:40.640
because Lava would be when it actually comes into&nbsp;
the open. Anyways, the fact that Oda basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:49.360
has thrown these two Yonko into literal hell&nbsp;
is pretty extreme I think. Not at all what I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:56.560
would have expected. The implication here seems&nbsp;
pretty clear also: These two people are gonna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:02.480
be painfully dissolved in an instant, never&nbsp;
to be seen again. And to top this all off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:08.480
the two cracks the Yonko made in the crust,&nbsp;
cause an underwater eruption of the volcano,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:16.720
that used to be Onigashima, as if to say: Yes&nbsp;
this is the end of the emperors Kaido and Big mom.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:22.880
This message is driven home even harder, when the&nbsp;
narrator corrects his initial mistake of declaring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:29.920
Kaido the victor. The actual winner is Luffy. On&nbsp;
top of that, Kaido also finally had closure in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:36.800
last chapter, realising that Luffy is indeed&nbsp;
JoyBoy, bringing closure to his big goal of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:42.480
finding someone strong enough to defeat him. The&nbsp;
straw hats and the rest of the alliance celebrate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:50.000
chopper starts treating patients, including my&nbsp;
man Zoro, who seems to be in a truly dangerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.040
condition here. And Yamato gets the remaining&nbsp;
beast pirates to surrender, while Momo carries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.040 --> 00:03:01.680
a whole delegation of the scabbards and Hiyori to&nbsp;
the Flower capital, declaring Kaido's defeat and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:08.240
announcing the new Shogun of Wano.&nbsp;
Oh, also a major shoutout to Franky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:13.280
who is the only straw hat that really looks like&nbsp;
he could still easily keep going after all this.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:21.040
And so really, this entire chapter is screaming&nbsp;
that this fight is over the Yonko are dead.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:27.520
The big question of course is:&nbsp;
Is that actually true? Or is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:31.120
Oda-sensei throwing us one of&nbsp;
infamous red herrings here?

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:40.240
Does it really make sense for Kaido and Big Mom,&nbsp;
two characters in dire need of some redemption&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:46.960
and closure, to die burning to death in a&nbsp;
volcano? Kaido, who wants nothing more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:52.880
see JoyBoy and die an honourable death? And&nbsp;
Big Mom, who has no idea yet, that she has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:59.440
been terrorising her own people in her feeding&nbsp;
frenzies? I find that hard to believe. I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:05.200
it's also a bit suspicious that it wasn't Mount&nbsp;
Fuji the main volcano of the island didn't erupt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:12.160
but onigashima at an angle. And the narrator,&nbsp;
who hasn't been super reliable recently either,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:17.280
hasn't declared either of them dead.&nbsp;
Also Kaido has a literal fire form.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:25.360
What I'm getting at here, is that I strongly&nbsp;
believe that we will see both Kaido and Big Mom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:32.000
emerge from this magma pit, possible through Mount&nbsp;
Fuji. Maybe strongly believe is a bit too much,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:40.080
I really hope to see this. However, not because&nbsp;
I think Kaido will activate his super ultra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:46.880
awakening and attack Luffy again. I really think&nbsp;
that the fight between the alliance and the Yonko&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:53.840
is over. Luffy has been recognised&nbsp;
by Kaido. And most importantly it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:59.680
doesn't look like Luffy will be able to do&nbsp;
any fighting whatsoever for quite some time.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:07.600
What I would much rather see, is a cathartic&nbsp;
ending for Kaido's arc. I've mentioned that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:12.720
before in my character analysis on him, but I&nbsp;
really feel like the best ending for him would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:19.120
be defending an incapacitated Luffy against some&nbsp;
external force, like the Marines or Blackbeard.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:26.000
But no matter if Kaido comes back or&nbsp;
not, I personally think that this was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:34.400
by far the most epic and awesome battle we have&nbsp;
witnessed in the story. We saw Luffy and Kaido&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:42.320
grow and change over many many chapters. Kaido&nbsp;
has literally been fighting non-stop for over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:46.800
70 chapters. He has faced off against&nbsp;
the scabbards, against the supernova,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:53.360
against Yamato and then against Luffy. He&nbsp;
has shown why he is the strongest creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:59.200
giving us both a broad variety of&nbsp;
fantastic attacks and fighting skills,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:06.720
but even more importantly a crazy character arc&nbsp;
throughout the fight, that taught us more and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:13.040
more about his motives and character, making his&nbsp;
ultimate defeat against luffy's final punch feel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:20.640
truly cathartic. It forced Luffy to surpass his&nbsp;
limits and himself over and over again to actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:26.880
earn the title of Emperor, that he got before the&nbsp;
arc, as did every single straw hat along the way.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:36.160
I know that battles and characters are a&nbsp;
very subjective matter, but to me personally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:43.200
Kaido is my favorite villain in the story at the&nbsp;
moment. I just hope he sticks around a bit longer.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:51.520
This has by far been the longest arc&nbsp;
and battle in the history of one piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:55.760
and especially when reading it back to&nbsp;
back without all the weekly discussions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.760 --> 00:07:01.840
and expectations built up, I find&nbsp;
it to be One Piece at its best.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:06.240
This is driven home by Tama and Tenguyama,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:11.920
who are heavily featured in this chapter as well.&nbsp;
We are being reminded of Yasu and his sacrifice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:16.160
all the events to even the way for&nbsp;
the raid to happen in the first place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:22.080
and all the people who were putting their&nbsp;
hopes and dreams into Luffy to free Wano.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:27.840
This chapter also set up a lot of things for the&nbsp;
future. Let me start with Zoro and Luffy. Both of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:34.000
them are completely out after pushing themselves&nbsp;
to the absolute limit. And while I think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:39.920
Luffy will have to be awake for the final big&nbsp;
banquet, that surely will have to happen at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:47.120
end of the wano arc, I'm not so sure if Zoro will&nbsp;
be waking up any time soon. As I've speculated in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:53.840
my Elbaf preview video, I think there is a really&nbsp;
good chance, that the two strongest straw hats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:58.640
might be out for the first part of the next&nbsp;
arc, giving room for the rest of the crew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:06.720
to shine and grow more. I'm actually super&nbsp;
curious to find out how taxing gear 5 will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:14.480
be for Luffy and how hard or easy it will be&nbsp;
for him to go into that form again. I suspect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:20.960
it might not be that Luffy can now just use&nbsp;
this form whenever, but has to master it first.

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:29.840
I also can't wait for an update to the Straw hat&nbsp;
bounties soon. That news bird with the new posters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:37.360
is always a major highlight of every single arc&nbsp;
for me. In fact, I do have a bounty myself. 58M&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:44.640
Berries for the 580.000 awesome people of you that&nbsp;
are subscribed. I'm very far from reaching Luffy's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:50.800
level or any of the straw hats really, but I am&nbsp;
determined to at least come for Treble's head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:55.440
who has 99M. So please help&nbsp;
me with that, by subscribing.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:59.840
Yamato is another big factor&nbsp;
in this chapter for me. In case&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:05.360
you've been around that long, you know&nbsp;
that I wanted Yamato to become a straw hat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:10.560
ever since their introduction. I would&nbsp;
be seriously hurt if it didn't happen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:17.520
after all the hints we have gotten for it. And in&nbsp;
this chapter, the beast pirates even acknowledge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:23.840
her as part of the alliance. Yamato is the one&nbsp;
who catches Luffy and who continued his fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:31.920
with Kaido until he got back on his feet.&nbsp;
I think we will get an answer to that soon.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:40.720
There is of course the cliffhanger with Denjiro,&nbsp;
who proclaims the next Shogun of Wano. Will it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:48.480
be Momo or will it be Hiyori? If it is Hiyori,&nbsp;
then Momo will keep sailing with the straw hats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:53.680
100%. And given that he has Kaido's powers&nbsp;
and is now at least physically grown up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:58.640
I would have no issue with that at all. And&nbsp;
hell I'll even give him that he has grown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:04.160
up personality wise as well. He has become a&nbsp;
true leader, made hard decisions for himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:10.560
showed real courage and saved his people. If&nbsp;
HE became the new Shogun, that would of course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:16.880
also be ironic, because Wano would get another&nbsp;
Dragon ruler, but this time a good one.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:22.880
Other than that, it's crazy that despite all&nbsp;
the celebration and seeming end to the fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:28.960
I still find it very hard to believe somehow that&nbsp;
wano will be wrapping up any time soon. There is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:34.640
still so many lose ends, the government waiting&nbsp;
outside the border, questions to be answered...I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:39.920
don't know. I'd like to think that there&nbsp;
is at least an Act IV waiting for us here.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:43.840
If you want to get a full thoughts and&nbsp;
analysis on Luffy's battle with Kaido,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:46.560
you really shouldn't skip this video right here.

